  "number": "1.6",
  "title": "Exercises",
  "body": " Exercises    Exercise tags. The tags below identify the primary outcomes and competency types for each exercise group. Individual problems may also involve earlier outcomes.    Matrices  Primary outcomes. U1-LO3. Competencies. P.   Nicholson 2.1.3(f)  Nicholson 2.1.8(b)  Nicholson 2.1.15(b)     Matrix-vector multiplication  Primary outcomes. U1-LO4. Competencies. P+R.   Nicholson 2.2.2(b)  Nicholson 2.2.3(b)  Nicholson 2.2.11(d)     Linear and affine maps  Primary outcomes. U1-LO5, U1-LO7. Competencies. P+C+R.   Nicholson 2.6.2(b)  Nicholson 2.6.13(b)     Matrix multiplication  Primary outcomes. U1-LO6. Competencies. P+R.   Nicholson 2.3.1(b)  Nicholson 2.3.3(b)  Nicholson 2.3.5(b)  Nicholson 2.3.16(b)     Additional applied and computational problems  These exercises connect the main Unit 1 ideas: vectors as data, cosine similarity, weighted averages, matrix-vector products, geometric matrix actions, composition, affine maps, and code interpretation. Solutions are collected in Appendix .   Word-count vectors and cosine similarity   Use the dictionary linear , matrix , data . Let     Compute the cosine similarity between and each document vector.  Rank the documents by cosine similarity.  Explain why has cosine similarity with .  Which document is orthogonal to ?  What does that orthogonality mean in terms of the dictionary words?  Compute the Euclidean distance from to each . Does the distance ranking match the cosine ranking?   Tags.  [U1-LO1, U1-LO2 | C+R | Core]     Weighted average of value vectors   Let and let    Compute .  Explain why this is a weighted average.  Which value vector receives the largest weight?   Tags.  [U1-LO8 | P+C | Core]     Attention bridge: hand scores versus   Use the token attention activity with tokens small , red , bird . Let      Compute the three dot products     Put the key vectors as rows of the matrix Compute .   Explain why the entries of are the same scores from part (a).  Normalize the scores by dividing by their sum. What is the weight vector ?   Tags.  [U1-LO1, U1-LO4, U1-LO8 | C+R | Core]     Rows measure; columns contribute   Let    Compute using row dot products.  Compute as a linear combination of the columns of .  In this example, what does the first row of measure?  In this example, what do the coordinates tell you in the column-combination view?   Tags.  [U1-LO4 | P+R | Core]     The unit-square visualization   Let    Compute and .  Compute .   Apply to the four corners of the unit square:    Sketch the image of the unit square.  Which two transformed edges leaving the origin are the columns of ?   Tags.  [U1-LO5, U1-LO8 | C+R | Core]     Transformation matching   Match each matrix with the correct geometric description.     Reflection across the -axis.  Projection onto the -axis.  Horizontal stretch.  Horizontal shear.  counterclockwise rotation.  Reflection across the line .   For each match, briefly justify your answer by describing what happens to and .  Tags.  [U1-LO5 | C+R | Core]     Composition order: versus   Let    Compute .  Compute .  Are and equal?  Which product represents apply first, then apply ?  Explain geometrically why the two orders produce different results.   Tags.  [U1-LO6 | P+R | Core]     Affine but not linear   Consider the transformation    Compute .  Explain why cannot be written in the form for any matrix .   Write in the affine form    Is linear, affine but not linear, or neither?   Tags.  [U1-LO7 | C+R | Core]     Code interpretation: sorting similarity scores   Consider the code:  import numpy as np doc_names = np.array([\"D1\", \"D2\", \"D3\"]) scores = np.array([1.0, 0.5, 0.0]) ranking = doc_names[np.argsort(scores)[::-1]] ranking   What is the value of ranking ?  What does np.argsort(scores) return?  What does [::-1] do?  What is being ranked?  Is this ranking based on direction, distance, or alphabetical order?   Tags.  [U1-LO2, U1-LO8 | R+T | Core]     Transformer shape check   Suppose a sequence of token vectors is stored in a matrix Let and define A later weighting step produces an attention-weight matrix , and the attention output is    What are the shapes of , , and ?  What is the shape of ?  What is the shape of ?  What is the shape of ?  What is the shape of ?  What does the -entry of compute?  Which product forms the weighted averages of value vectors?  In this convention, are token vectors stored as rows or columns of ?   Tags.  [U1-LO3, U1-LO6, U1-LO8 | R+T | Core]     "
