  "body": "  Consider the function on the unit square   Find the absolute maximum and minimum values of on .    The set is closed and bounded, so we can apply .  We start by finding the critical points of in the interior of , i.e., on the set . We compute that . These two quantities vanish simultaneously at the point , which is therefore the only critical point of . At this point .  Now we check the boundary of . The boundary is the union of four curves, and so we can parameterize these curves, and find the critical points of the parameterization, to determine potential absolute minima and maxima on these curves (treating the corners of separately).  On the bottom edge , the function takes the form . The only critical point of the expression occurs at , and . Similarly, on the top edge , the function takes the form . As for the bottom edge, the only critical point of the expression occurs at , and . On the left edge , the function takes the form . The only critical point of the expression occurs when , and . Similarly, on the right edge , the function takes the form . The only critical point of this expression occurs when , and . Among the boundary critical points, the smallest value occurs at , where has value , and the largest value occurs at , where has value .  Finally, we must check the value of the function at the four corners , , , and . We calculate that , , , and .  Comparing all values, we see that the absolute maximum of on occurs at , with maximum value , and the absolute minimum occurs at , with minimum value .   "
